formation Integration Theory offers a broader consciousness framework in which subjective experience is tied to integrated informational structure within complexes, with both quantity and quality specified by integrated information and effective-information relationships.\",\n      \"heading\": \"Integrated Experience\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"body\": \"The shared concept is not that these sources use the same theory, but that both treat conscious subjectivity as structured by relations among specialized processes: S-ART focuses on self-related networks and practice-related modulation, while IIT focuses on integrated complexes and qualia-space structure.\",\n      \"heading\": \"Synthesis Boundary\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"source_ids\": [\n    \"source-05-self-awareness-self-regulation-and-self-transcendence-s-art-a-framework-for-unde-w2005022581--615ee4e1923f\",\n    \"source-01-an-information-integration-theory-of-consciousness-w2114900706--09db8f102f39\"\n  ],\n  \"structure_type\": \"wiki\",\n  \"title\": \"Self-Processing and Integrated Conscious Experience\",\n  \"topic_id\": \"topic-self-processing-conscious-integration\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
